hi this is pressure Locker this puzzle  makes for a fun question to ask your  friends at parties and it's also used as  an interview question so imagine you  have ten coins and three cups your job  is to place the ten coins into the three  cups so that each cup contains an odd  number of coins give this problem a try  and when you're ready keep watching the  video for the solution so I would  approach the question mathematically by  looking for the ways you can add three  numbers up to ten these are also known  as the partitions of 10 so you could  have 1 plus 1 plus 8 which equals 10 you  could also write this as 1 plus 8 plus 1  or 8 plus 1 plus 1 but I'm going to  write the sums in increasing order so I  don't have to write every single  possibility we'll come up with the  different ways that we can add three  numbers up to 10 and write them in  increasing order there are only a few  number of ways and what you'll notice in  every single possibility one of the  numbers at least one of the numbers will  be an even number so if we want to have  all three cups be odd numbers we  actually have an impossibility now just  in case I didn't write down all the  possibilities I'm going to prove this as  well so suppose we try and put an odd  number into each cup so we have 2x plus  1 2 I plus 1 and 2z plus 1 we want the  sum of the coins to equal 10 and that  means we have 2 times some number X plus  y plus Z equals 7 now clearly this is  going to be impossible because we can't  have 2 times a whole positive number be  equal to an odd number which is 7 so we  cannot solve this problem in the  traditional way by trying to partition  the 10 coins so that each cup has an odd  number of coins so we're going to have  to think creatively  so let's take one of the partitions two  three and five we'll put two coins into  the left cup three coins into the milk  up and we'll put five the remaining five  coins into the third cup so how can we  get all three cups to have an odd number  of coins well here's the trick we take  the middle cup and place it on top of  the first cup so now that middle cup  still has three coins that's an odd  number the first cup actually contains  two plus three coins which is five and  five is an odd number and the cup on the  right contains five so that also is an  odd number so this solution corresponds  to the partition of two three and five  which is one even number and two odd  numbers so we could similarly do this  solution whenever we have one even  number and two odd numbers we will put  the cup which has one of the cups which  has an odd number in one of the cups  which has an even number so with one one  and eight we would put one of the cups  which has one on top of one of the cup  which has eight so we can similarly do  this kind of solution whenever we have  one even number and two odd numbers now  if we have to if we have all even  numbers that's not going to generate us  a solution because an even plus and even  will still be an even we'd also expand  the solution so if we had zero one and  nine and then we put the cup with one in  side of the cup which has zero we'll  also get a solution where all the cups  have an odd number so if you expand zero  you also get a couple more solutions did  you figure it out thanks for watching  this video please subscribe to my  channel I make videos on math and game  theory you can catch me on my blog mind  your decisions which you can follow on  Facebook Google+ and patreon you can  also catch me on social media at  pressure Locker now if you like this  video please check on my books there are  links in the video description
 

